{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1201848-comparing-emphereals","id":1201848,"title":"Comparing Emphereals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-31T21:36:12-07:00","id":1201848,"title":"Comparing Emphereals","content":"There are now a fair amount of Emphereals in the game now. <br /> <br /> We have Ghosts, Spirits, Chthonians, Angels, Goetics, Gumoths, Acamoths, Strix, Belial Familiars, Qausimilli, Lilitu, Souls, Hedge Ghosts, Loyal Servants, Supernal Beings (Demons, Angels, Fae, Shades, Totems).<br /> <br /> So how do they stack up against each other? How would they interact, and what can be done to improve emphereals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T22:22:02-07:00","id":1201854,"title":"","content":"Well, some of the beings you list aren't ephemeral entities, strictly speaking. (And I don't recognize some of them - Lilitu? Loyal Servants?)<br /> <br /> Anyways, so far the angels of the God-Machine have enjoyed the most attention, with things like Incepts and the implied ability to sidestep some Manifestations thanks the God-Machine providing angelic Cover. Ghosts might get similar attention in Geist 2E. If we include homebrew, Acrozatarim brought up Noble Numina for spirit nobles to use, in the Werewolf forums, which pack quite a punch. Oh, and speaking of Werewolf, aren't idigam technically ephemeral entities too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T23:48:27-07:00","id":1201862,"title":"","content":"Lilitu are vampires. Idigam are spirits. Belial Familiars would probably be a wounded spirit or ghost.<br /> <br /> I'll cut the list down.<br /> <br /> Ghosts, spirits, angels, goetics, maybe Chthonians, maybe gulmoths, maybe acamoths, maybe hedge ghosts. But add idigam.<br /> <br /> They don't, for the most part, interact unless they're meant to somehow. The ghost of a shaman may be able to do things with spirits, just like a spirit of death may be able to use Essence Thief on a ghost. Angel-hunting isn't really a thing, so I suspect when spirits or ghosts come across an angel doing something, they are curious, but otherwise leave them alone. It's possible an angel might be posing as something, a certain ghost in the underworld, or spirit in the Shadow. In which case whatever their 'job' there can have great effect (moreso, I think, on spirits, if only because I have no idea what happens in the Underworld but it doesn't seem to be an ecosystem). Angels are sent to do things, so an Angel sent to deal with shadows is going to do something, and it's probably the usual kind of chaos that kicks off plots for mortal, mage, or werewolf games. But in this case, it would not be a spirit interacting with an angel, so much as a spirit interacting with an angel it thinks is a spirit. Gulmoth and acamoth seem like they might interact with this stuff (Gulmoth with spirits, acamoth with Goetia) but I don't think it's limited that way, a gulmoth could be an entirely physical entity, and an acamoth might not need Goetia to do what it does. I say could more because I have no idea, they haven't been expanded on, but in this case the Abyss would be like the Inferno, infecting things, but instead of 'evil' you get 'things from the abyss.' They corrupt, usurp, then spread..<br /> <br /> In case it's not obvious by now, these guys generally aren't going to be like 'Who you tryin to get crazy with, ese? Don'choo know I'm loco?' then Blast at each other.<br /> <br /> Idigam are a big old corrupting force, however, and have swarms of things willing to be loyal to them, or made to be loyal by them. They are chaos in the violent order of the predator's playground. They don't seem aggressive to you unless you're trying to stop them from becoming what they want, but they often have impact on the world around them in general. That's before you get to the scary stuff. Like if an idigam starts seeing these angels and thinking they'll make better servants he'll start shoving them into people's bodies, or tainting them in other ways. You have a lot of plot material here. And no one should have a, 'Well one side just destroys the other.' It's something the players should be drawn into.<br /> <br /> At higher levels, things seem to work easier, there's less entities, mostly sticking to their own domains. Luna seems to (among other things) defend earth from foreign spiritual entities that may wreck the world, or take it from her. Mattaron, an angel, does something similar, watching for more physical threats (like meteors) and stopping them if they threaten too much of the God Machine's work. They don't seem to interact, Mattaron does what the God Machine says and casual conversation with other entities doesn't seem to be high on priority. These are alien entities, they're not human or human-like, or whatever it is when an anime depicts inanimate objects as people. Still, Mattaron, being a simple entity, is easy to understand. Listen to the music of the spheres, if there's a threat, work with other angels to analyze the threat, then send the numbers to someone else who makes the decisions. His life seems like a robots would, which makes sense, as that's effectively what he is. I even keep attributing it as a male, but it is firmly an 'it.'<br /> <br /> Luna is harder, I think she's got a lot more Influences under her belt than most spirits her size, and it's likely she's mad. Consider most spirits are probably called crazy, due to their alienness, but their actions make sense if you know the influences, the resonances. It's easy to imagine playing a spirit in a video game. But Luna may be actually crazy, so there's no way to tell if the things she does are because she's a powerful spirit that meddles with the world, or because she's crazy and can do these things. I have to assume she knows of angels, what with the things they have on the moon, we have seen no or little evidence that she cares or did anything about it.<br /> <br /> Some things that may help.<ul><li>What do Goetia want? Spirits are easy, ghosts are easy, angels are easy. There's loads of Goetia, and they seem to just re-enact memories. Some seem like consciences (this is more obvious, they want to give advice, sort of). They aren't ephemerals, but what do Supernals do between summonings from mages?</li> <li>Why do spirits start the feudal thing? I'm guessing from a setting explanation it's the Iron Pyramid at work, the core reason is fine as a mystery, but why does a Rank 5 spirit say, 'Give me tithes,' rather than 'I'm going to eat you?'</li> <li>Some expansion on Influences. We're seeing a much wider variety, but whenever I see something obscure like 'Influence: Infrastructure,' I'm at a loss for how it would come into play beyond Strengthen giving it more dots.</li> <li>Along with that, a brief guide to making entity-specific Numina. Why they might have them, that they are rare or unique to that entity. We don't have much in the books about setting building stuff.</li> <li>A mortal, a mage, and a werewolf are exploring the deep shadow. What's the deep shadow? And sooner or later they encounter a Rank 6 entity. They can't tell this, however. But they feel something, they are in a colossal presence with Power off the charts. Does the very air around them thrum? Do these things seem beyond others of their kind? Do they still do the feudal thing? Can you track a powerful Rank 6, 7, and up by following those who give it tithes? Would you find some great spirit court-city? Or something that, when they return, no one else believes because it's so different from the common understanding of these things?</li> </ul>Like I said, because this is dealing with 'high rank' stuff, a lot of it is easily taken out of context. Chronicles of Darkness is Dark with mystery, and Why Luna does everything she does and the God Machine's origin shouldn't necessarily be answered in a book. But there are things that are more reasonable to answer without giving a character sheet. Astral Realms did it very well, showing off Dahhak, the entirety of his 'character sheet' being, 'Rank: 8.' followed by a list of what he's capable of and is likely to do or not do. That's fantastic. In fact some of these answers are already answered for with the Aeons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2018, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}